In article <3241f9c8.2108181@SantaAna01.news.internex.net>,
ecsi@ix.netcom.com (A.H. Ongun) writes:
:We have a need to capture an X-term window and send it to a printer.
:	1.  Is there a program/utility that can accomplish this?

  Since this is posted (among other newsgroups) to the OpenVMS newsgroups,
  I'll assume DECwindows or DECwindows Motif running under OpenVMS.  If so,
  there is a supported <print screen> application integrated directly into
  the standard session manager -- see the session manager menus.

  If the <print screen> option is not visible in your current DECwindows
  or DECwindows Motif menu configuration, you will have to add it via the
  menu customization options -- see the <Options> menu <Menus> option.

	--

  The operating system name, the release, and relevent products -- in this
  case, the windowing system and version -- are often useful to the folks
  that are answering questions here.

